1. DEFINITIONS

1.1  "Work" means everything in this repository authored by the copyright
     holder, including: source code; the extraction contract and its field,
     family, category, and routing definitions; the operator runbooks and the
     copy-ready agent role briefs, whether written by hand or produced by a
     generator in this repository; the quality rules and their tolerances; the
     generation configuration; the database schemas; the documentation; and the
     selection, arrangement, and structure of the whole.

1.2  "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, adapted from,
     translated from, reorganised from, or otherwise derived from the Work or
     any Substantial Portion of it, in any medium and in any programming or
     natural language. Rewriting the Work into a different language, framework,
     or prompt format produces a Derivative Work.

1.3  "Substantial Portion" means any part of the Work that reflects the
     copyright holder's selection, arrangement, or expression rather than an
     unprotectable idea. Without limiting that meaning, each of the following is
     a Substantial Portion on its own:
       (a)  the text of any extractor, adjudicator, normalizer, or research role
            brief, in whole or in part;
       (b)  the record and coverage contracts, including the field list, the
            controlled vocabularies, the record families, and the rules binding
            a value to its printed location and evidence;
       (c)  the validator, comparison, adjudication, and publication logic and
            the conditions under which each refuses work;
       (d)  the quality rule set, its identifiers, and its tolerances;
       (e)  the identity, sponsor-family, and manager-research workflow and its
            file contracts;
       (f)  the repository structure, folder guides, and manifest scheme.

1.4  "Commercial Use" means any use by or for the benefit of a business,
     including internal use in the ordinary course of a business, and including
     use that produces data, analysis, models, reports, or products offered to
     any third party for consideration. Evaluation of the copyright holder for
     employment or engagement is not Commercial Use.

1.5  "Third-Party Material" means material in this repository that the copyright
     holder did not author. See section 7.


2. PERMISSION GRANTED WITHOUT PAYMENT

Subject to sections 3 to 6, any person may, at no charge:

2.1  read, download, and retain a copy of the Work;

2.2  run the Work locally to verify the claims made in its documentation;

2.3  use the Work for personal study, academic teaching, and academic research
     that is published without charge; and

2.4  evaluate the Work, and the copyright holder's capability through it, for
     the purpose of deciding whether to employ or engage the copyright holder.

The permission in this section is limited to the acts it names. Every other
right stays with the copyright holder.


